---
/**
 * Copyright, Trademarks and Takedown Policy
 *
 * @description
 * 版权与知识产权声明：站内原创内容（文字/数据/图表/计算）的使用许可、第三方商标的指示性使用说明、
 * 通知—删除（takedown / DMCA 式）流程与联系邮箱、反向侵权举报。
 */
import MarketingLayout from '@/layouts/MarketingLayout.astro';
import { siteConfig, company } from '@/config';

const { legal } = siteConfig;
const year = new Date().getFullYear();
---

<MarketingLayout
  title="Copyright, Trademarks and Takedown Policy"
  description="What is protected on EV Hub, how our content and calculated data may be reused, how third-party trademarks are used, and the procedure for sending a copyright takedown notice."
>
  <section class="py-section">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <header class="mb-12">
        <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-text">Copyright, Trademarks and Takedown Policy</h1>
        <p class="mt-4 text-text-muted">Last updated: {legal.lastUpdated}</p>
      </header>

      <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none dark:prose-invert">
        <h2>1. What this policy covers</h2>
        <p>
          This policy explains what intellectual property exists on {siteConfig.name}, what you may do with it, how we
          handle third-party rights, and how a rights holder can ask us to remove material. It applies to everything
          published at electricvehiclehub.net — articles, model pages, market breakdowns, tables, charts, calculated
          figures, images and page design.
        </p>

        <h2>2. Our content</h2>
        <p>
          Unless stated otherwise, the written content, editorial structure, data tables, charts and calculated
          figures on this site are © {year} {company.legalName}. All rights reserved.
        </p>
        <p><strong>You may, without asking:</strong></p>
        <ul>
          <li>read, print and share individual pages for your own reference;</li>
          <li>
            quote up to a few paragraphs or a single table, or cite a calculated figure, in editorial, academic or
            commercial analysis, provided you credit {siteConfig.name} and link to the page you used;
          </li>
          <li>link to any page from your website, newsletter or social channel.</li>
        </ul>
        <p><strong>You may not, without written permission:</strong></p>
        <ul>
          <li>republish whole articles or substantial parts of them, on any platform, in any language;</li>
          <li>scrape, harvest or machine-copy the site in bulk, or rebuild our dataset for resale or redistribution;</li>
          <li>present our content, or a lightly edited version of it, as your own or as a work for hire;</li>
          <li>use {siteConfig.name} content to train or fine-tune a commercial model where the output competes with this site.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Machine-readable access for search and AI answer engines is permitted as described in our{' '}
          <a href="/llms.txt">llms.txt</a> file; that permission is for indexing and citation, not for wholesale
          reproduction.
        </p>

        <h2>3. Calculated data and figures</h2>
        <p>
          Our landed-cost breakdowns, duty and VAT totals, and market comparisons are original calculations built from
          published tariff schedules and freight inputs. You are welcome to cite a figure with attribution and a link.
          If you reuse the numbers, please also carry the caveats that appear with them on the page — the estimates
          depend on assumptions that are stated in our{' '}
          <a href="/landed-cost-methodology/">landed-cost methodology</a> and change over time.
        </p>

        <h2>4. Third-party trademarks</h2>
        <p>
          Vehicle brand names, model names, marques, logos and trade dress belong to their respective owners.
          {siteConfig.name} uses them solely to identify the products being described or compared — a nominative,
          descriptive use. Its appearance on this site does not imply that any manufacturer, importer or dealer has
          approved, sponsored or endorsed us, or that we act as their agent. We are not a dealer, importer or
          distributor, and we do not sell vehicles.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you believe a mark is used in a way that misleads readers or infringes your rights, write to us at{' '}
          <a href={`mailto:${legal.legalEmail}`}>{legal.legalEmail}</a> and we will review the usage and, where
          appropriate, adjust it.
        </p>

        <h2>5. Third-party photographs and illustrations</h2>
        <p>
          Photographs used on this site are either freely licensed (CC0, CC BY or CC BY-SA) or, in some cases, supplied
          by manufacturers and other third parties for identification purposes. Full attribution for freely licensed
          photographs is published on our <a href="/image-credits/">Image Credits and Copyright</a> page. We claim no
          ownership of third-party imagery and remove it on request.
        </p>

        <h2>6. Notice and takedown procedure</h2>
        <p>
          If you hold the rights to material published here and believe it is used without permission, send a notice to{' '}
          <a href={`mailto:${legal.legalEmail}`}>{legal.legalEmail}</a> including:
        </p>
        <ol>
          <li>your name, organisation (if any), postal address and email address;</li>
          <li>identification of the work you say is infringed, with a link to the original where it is published;</li>
          <li>
            the URL of each page on this site that carries the material, precise enough for us to locate it (page URL
            and, for images, the image URL);
          </li>
          <li>a statement that you have a good-faith belief the use is not authorised by the rights holder, its agent or the law;</li>
          <li>
            a statement that the information in your notice is accurate and that you are the rights holder or
            authorised to act for them;
          </li>
          <li>your signature (electronic is fine).</li>
        </ol>
        <p>
          <strong>What happens next.</strong> We acknowledge notices within 5 business days. Where a claim is credible
          on its face, we remove or replace the material promptly — usually while the review is still running — and
          confirm the outcome to you in writing. We keep a record of the notice, the action taken and the date. If we
          believe the use is lawful and properly licensed, we will explain why, with our evidence, rather than simply
          ignoring the notice.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Counter-notice.</strong> If your material is removed and you believe the removal was mistaken (for
          example, you can show the licence we relied on), write to the same address. We will restore the material if
          you can substantiate your right to use it.
        </p>

        <h2>7. Reporting infringement of our content</h2>
        <p>
          If you find our content republished elsewhere without attribution — including whole-article copies, scraped
          model pages, or our tables and figures presented as another site's work — please tell us at{' '}
          <a href={`mailto:${legal.legalEmail}`}>{legal.legalEmail}</a> with the URL. We pursue these cases, and we
          appreciate the tips.
        </p>

        <h2>8. Related policies</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><a href="/terms/">Terms of Use</a></li>
          <li><a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a></li>
          <li><a href="/cookies/">Cookie Policy</a></li>
          <li><a href="/disclaimer/">Disclaimer</a></li>
          <li><a href="/image-credits/">Image Credits and Copyright</a></li>
          <li><a href="/editorial-independence/">Editorial Independence Policy</a></li>
          <li><a href="/accessibility/">Accessibility Statement</a></li>
          <li><a href="/contact/">Contact</a></li>
        </ul>

        <p class="text-sm text-text-muted">
          Questions about this policy: <a href={`mailto:${legal.legalEmail}`}>{legal.legalEmail}</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</MarketingLayout>
